{"created": "2026-10-15T07:50:10.998117+00:00", "modified": "2026-10-15T07:50:11.370176+00:00", "id": 23387442, "conceptrecid": "23387441", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23387442", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.23387441", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23387442", "metadata": {"title": "Counterexamples to Satoh's SL(2) representation-filtration conjecture", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.23387442", "publication_date": "2026-10-15", "description": "We give explicit counterexamples to the equality of the integral Andreadakis filtration A_n(k) and the SL(2,C) representation filtration D_n(k) formulated in Satoh's 2018 Oberwolfach report. D_n(k) acts on the whole quotient J/J^(k+1) in the rational algebra of individual matrix-entry functions. Elementary automorphisms lie in D_n(5) minus A_n(5) for every n&gt;=4 and in D_n(6) minus A_n(6) for every n&gt;=3, refuting the universal equality at every rank in the source's stated range. The proof uses a classical degree-five Lie identity, explicitly credited to Burde arXiv:1411.0950v2 equation(4) and Theorem4.14, with its Razmyslov attribution reported through that inspected source; the degree-six identity is a weighted substitution. No new PI identity or general PI method is claimed. Actual ideal-power containments and integral Magnus coefficients supply a self-contained proof. Independent exact polynomial and finite integer-matrix computations supplement it. Degree 5 at rank 3, every-degree failure, larger matrix sizes, trace algebras and the ordinary IA lower-central-series conjecture are not claimed. The bounded priority audit located no verified older complete application to this exact equality; historical firstness, exhaustive novelty clearance and continuously open status through 2026 remain uncertified. Complete final 2017/2021 Satoh journal texts and some related 2025/2026 journal texts were inaccessible; inspected public preprints, shorter sources and abstracts are distinguished in the archive. It preserves the unchanged original candidate and independent mathematical/priority reports, source-hash ledgers and verification code, without redistributing third-party full texts. AI tools were used extensively in development, verification, source investigation and writing. This is an unrefereed preprint without independent human peer review; internal AI reviews are not human peer review.", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kriebel, Alec", "affiliation": "Independent researcher", "orcid": "0009-0001-9320-500X"}], "keywords": ["free group automorphisms", "Andreadakis filtration", "representation algebra", "SL(2)", "polynomial identity", "Magnus expansion", "counterexample"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/681", "relation": "isSupplementedBy", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.4171/OWR/2018/2", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1607.05411v2", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}, {"identifier": "10.1017/S0013091516000456", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.2140/pjm.2021.312.477", "relation": "references", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "https://arxiv.org/abs/1411.0950v2", "relation": "references", "scheme": "url"}], "version": "1.0", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "23387441"}}]}}, "title": "Counterexamples to Satoh's SL(2) representation-filtration conjecture", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/23387442", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23387442", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/23387442?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23387442", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23387442", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.23387442", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/233874